From b2f5aa0ca0d8b05f72f249ee56f6c5deb811f141 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 14:47:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Net play: HOST is a button, JOIN is a row marked HOSTING -
 roles declared, not raced for

Both machines came up as host, exactly as they had both come up as
player 2 before: two versions that settled the roles from who dialled
whom, and two people testing a panel click on both of them. This is the
F7 / F8 model the keys had before the panel, which worked, with the
typing taken out.

  [ CLICK HERE TO HOST A GAME ]         one pc clicks this
  or CLICK a pc below that is HOSTING:  the other sees it, clicks JOIN

The beacon carries a hosting byte (no / open / full), so a row reads
[CLICK to JOIN] ip  HOSTING, or  ip  online, not hosting - clicking the
latter says "on that pc, CLICK HOST first" instead of dialling and failing
two seconds later. A pc never heard from shows ? and can be tried; if it is
sitting idle at the panel it accepts and becomes player 2.

The host's screen says YOU ARE HOSTING - waiting for player 2, with the
mission arrows usable straight away and START appearing when somebody
joins. Player 2 leaving puts the host back to waiting, not back to the
list. The joiner's screen says JOINED - you are player 2 and that there is
nothing to click.

Vertical pitch is 10 px throughout, every line at a fixed y, and the
headings are one line of forty characters: the overlap was the host
heading wrapping onto the mission row. Six rows fit, and the status has
four lines.

